See bug & glitches doc for more information on problems and fixes.


Version Key Guide:

X.Y.Zb#

X is the major version (1: Alpha, 2: Beta, 3: Final)
Y is the minor changes from the major version (e.g. 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 1.4)
Z is the incremental/patch changes and bug fixes (e.g. 1.1.1, 1.1.2, 1.1.3)

Sometimes there will be a minor fix: that is where the b# comes in. After a revision the b# goes up one and resets after a minor change. For example, v1.2.3 is a normal version
v1.2.3b45 would be a version (1.2.3) that has been revised with minuscule changes 45 times.
b stands for build and it will not be shown in a version name when at 1.

	
